---
import '../../styles/admin.css';
import '@fontsource/inter/400.css';
import '@fontsource/inter/500.css';
import '@fontsource/manrope/500.css';
import '@fontsource/manrope/700.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={new URL('admin/', Astro.site)} /><link
      rel="icon"
      href="/images/660ca351a18d35e961252c4a_jb-total--icon-32.png"
    /><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Dashboard concept | Total Tissue & Fitness</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="An interactive partner dashboard concept with fictional sample data. Changes are not saved."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="admin-body">
    <a class="admin-skip" href="#workspace-main">Skip to workspace</a>
    <header class="workspace-header">
      <a href="/" class="workspace-brand"
        ><img
          src="/images/optimized/total-tissue-logo.webp"
          alt="Total Tissue & Fitness"
          width="180"
          height="60"
        /></a
      >
      <div class="workspace-header-actions">
        <span class="status-pill">CONCEPT PREVIEW</span><a href="/">View website ↗</a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <main id="workspace-main" class="workspace-main">
      <div class="workspace-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">PARTNER WORKSPACE / A FIRST LOOK</p><h1>Practice dashboard</h1><p>
          Inquiries, service content, and the tools behind your practice.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="workspace-message concept-banner">
        <strong>Dashboard concept · fictional sample data · changes are not saved</strong><p>
          This is an interactive preview. No accounts are connected, no messages are sent, and every
          edit resets when you reload the page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <noscript
        ><p class="workspace-message">
          JavaScript is required to explore the interactive concept. No live operations are
          available here.
        </p></noscript
      >
      <div class="workspace-toolbar">
        <label class="compact-label"
          >Preview a future role<select id="preview-role"
            ><option value="owner">Practice owner</option><option value="partner">Partner</option
            ><option value="viewer">Read-only collaborator</option></select
          ></label
        ><p id="role-description">
          Concept: access to inquiries, service drafts, and team planning.
        </p><button id="reset-preview" class="quiet-button">Reset preview</button>
      </div>
      <div class="concept-metrics">
        <article>
          <span>Sample inquiries</span><strong id="sample-inquiry-count">03</strong><p>
            Fictional entries to explore
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span>Draft concepts</span><strong>02</strong><p>Try editing service copy</p>
        </article><article>
          <span>Future access</span><strong>03</strong><p>Proposed role levels</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <nav class="workspace-tabs" aria-label="Workspace sections">
        <a href="#inquiries">Inquiry inbox</a><a href="#service-drafts">Service drafts</a><a
          href="#resources">Practice resources</a
        ><a href="#access-plan">Access plan</a>
      </nav>
      <div id="workspace-message" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="preview-feedback"></div>
      <section id="inquiries" class="workspace-card">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">KEEP THE CONVERSATION MOVING</p><h2>Inquiry inbox</h2></div><label
            class="compact-label"
            >Show<select id="inquiry-filter"
              ><option value="all">All sample inquiries</option><option value="new">New</option
              ><option value="contacted">Contacted</option><option value="closed">Closed</option
              ></select
            ></label
          >
        </div><p class="workspace-muted">
          These people and messages are fictional. Status changes affect this preview only.
        </p><div id="inquiry-list" class="inquiry-list"></div>
      </section>
      <section id="service-drafts" class="workspace-card">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">SHAPE THE NEXT UPDATE</p><h2>Service drafts</h2></div><span
            class="status-pill">Demo · not saved</span
          >
        </div><p>
          Try adjusting the copy below, then preview the result. A future workflow could pass
          reviewed drafts to Claude for a website update.
        </p><div id="draft-list"></div>
      </section>
      <section id="resources" class="workspace-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">YOUR PRACTICE, CONNECTED</p><h2>Practice resources</h2><div
          class="resource-grid"
        >
          <a href="/book/"
            ><span>Existing client pathways</span><strong>Booking options ↗</strong></a
          ><a href="/manual-therapy/"
            ><span>Public service information</span><strong>Review manual therapy ↗</strong></a
          ><a href="https://www.synaptyxperformance.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            ><span>Our partner</span><strong>Synaptyx Health & Performance ↗</strong></a
          ><article>
            <span>Future website maintenance</span><strong>A clear handoff to Claude</strong><p>
              Review a draft, describe the desired outcome, and have Claude prepare a website change
              for approval. This concept has no connected publishing workflow.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="access-plan" class="workspace-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">DESIGNED FOR INDIVIDUAL ACCESS</p><h2>A place for every partner.</h2><p>
          Proposed permissions for a future secure dashboard. The role selector above only changes
          this demonstration; it does not authenticate or authorize anyone.
        </p><div class="access-table-wrap">
          <table class="access-table">
            <thead
              ><tr
                ><th scope="col">Future capability</th><th scope="col">Owner</th><th scope="col"
                  >Partner</th
                ><th scope="col">Read-only</th></tr
              ></thead
            ><tbody
              ><tr><th scope="row">Review inquiries</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr
                ><th scope="row">Update inquiry status</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td></tr
              ><tr><th scope="row">Prepare service drafts</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td></tr
              ><tr><th scope="row">Manage team access</th><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr><tr
                ><th scope="row">Approve publication</th><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr
              ></tbody
            >
          </table>
        </div><p class="workspace-muted">
          Future implementation: individual accounts, database-enforced roles, a private inquiry
          inbox, and a reviewed publishing process. Setup is deferred until the concept is approved.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="workspace-footer">Total Tissue & Fitness <span>Dashboard concept</span></footer>
    <script src="../../scripts/admin.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
